## The Challenge

The Indian denim market is crowded. On one side, you have cheap, unbranded jeans; on the other, expensive international giants (Levi's, Zara). The challenge was to build a local brand that didn't feel local. We needed to create an identity that felt premium, timeless, and "cool" enough for Gen Z, without mimicking Western brands. The goal was to turn "Made in India" from a manufacturing tag into a badge of pride.

