## Cedar Jeans: The Fabric of Confidence.

Redefining Indian Denim with Earthy Tones and Unapologetic Boldness.

Cedar Jeans

(2024)

## The Solution

### We steered away from the standard "industrial blue" cliché. Instead, we built the brand around "Earthy Confidence."

- **The Palette:** We used Cedar Brown, Forest Green, and Raw Canvas colors. This immediately signals "natural materials" and "durability" before the customer even touches the fabric.
- **The Logo:** We designed a "Stamp of Approval" style logo. It mimics old-school leather quality seals, instantly building trust and emphasizing the "Est. 2000" heritage feel.
- **The Typography:** We didn't just make a logo; we designed the whole business. We applied this clean look to menus, chopstick sleeves, takeout packaging, and billboards. Every item looks like it belongs to the same family.

![Cedar Jeans case study image](../../assets/projects/cedar-jeans/Colors.webp)

![Cedar Jeans case study image](../../assets/projects/cedar-jeans/Cedar-Secondary-Typography.webp)

![Cedar Jeans case study image](../../assets/projects/cedar-jeans/Cedar-5.webp)

## The results

### Cedar Jeans is not just a logo; it is a Retail-Ready System.

- **Scalable:** The "Stamp" identity works just as well on a tiny metal rivet button as it does on a huge highway hoarding.
- **Market Ready:** The packaging system (tags, bags, labels) is designed to look good on a shelf next to top-tier competitors.
- **Brand Voice:** We gave the brand a voice that isn't about fabric—it's about feeling. The "Your Curves, Your Confidence" campaign shifts the focus from the product to the person wearing it.

